That inequality is not a formal theorem from the board; it is a way of writing the lecture’s causal claim. Once it is true in practice, large firms acquire an implicit government guarantee. The mechanism the lecture stresses is then $\begin{aligned}
\text{large-firm failure}
&\Rightarrow
\text{threat to the system}
\Rightarrow
\text{likely bailout},\\
\text{likely bailout}
&\Rightarrow
\text{implicit guarantee}
\Rightarrow
\text{greater risk-taking}
\Rightarrow
\text{greater systemic risk}.\end{aligned}$

