p.src:
From there the lecture introduces a pair of terms that became especially prominent after the financial crisis of the 2000s: microprudential and macroprudential. Prudential here means regulation concerned with prudent standards of business conduct. The difference lies in the object of protection: $\begin{aligned}
\text{Microprudential regulation}
&\longrightarrow
\text{protect firms, households, and individual investors},\\
\text{Macroprudential regulation}
&\longrightarrow
\text{protect the system as a whole}.\end{aligned}$

