p.src:
That same idea is carried over to finance. In a competitive system, if everyone else is doing something shady, then one may feel compelled to do it too in order to survive. The lecture calls this a race to the bottom. In schematic form, $\begin{aligned}
\text{if others cheat}
\Rightarrow
\text{pressure to imitate}
\Rightarrow
\text{demand for enforceable rules}.\end{aligned}$

