p.src:
From there the lecture goes fully international. The problem is easy to state. If regulation is costly, then financial firms can move offshore. If they dislike U.S. rules, there is always the Bahamas or the Cayman Islands. So we are led to another causal chain: $\begin{aligned}
\text{tighter national regulation}
\Rightarrow
\text{offshore migration}
\Rightarrow
\text{need for international coordination}.\end{aligned}$

